@lang en
-- Tests of ie-repeal.l4: ss 2(2), 3(1), 3(2), 26 and 27.
-- Each rule is a conjunction or disjunction of the text's own conditions; each condition is varied alone.
-- "Before the repeal" is tested on both sides of the moment the repealing enactment comes into operation, and on the day itself where that day has no moment.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-operation-and-construction`
IMPORT `ie-repeal`

§ `Helpers: repealing enactments with a moment, and one with only a day`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`an Act expressed to come into operation on` d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` d
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`an Act that says nothing, passed on` d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on` d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `a statutory instrument`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST d

§ `A thing done before the repealing enactment`

-- with a moment: an Act expressed to come into operation on 2026-06-01 comes into operation at the end of 2026-05-31
#ASSERT     `a thing on` (YMD 2026 5 30) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT     `a thing on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `a thing on` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `a thing on` (YMD 2026 6 2)  `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- a statutory instrument that says nothing: the end of the day before the day it is made
#ASSERT     `a thing on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `a thing on` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- with no moment: an Act that says nothing, passed on 2026-06-01
#ASSERT     `a thing on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `a thing on` (YMD 2026 6 2)  `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `a thing on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) BECAUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether a thing done on that day precedes the commencement is not answered"
-- month end, leap day: an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 March 2024 comes into operation at the end of the leap day
#ASSERT     `a thing on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2024 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `a thing on` (YMD 2024 3 1)  `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2024 3 1))
-- a day not yet fixed refuses
#ASSERT REFUSED `a thing on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `precedes the commencement of the repealing enactment` (`Facts about an enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`, `what it says about commencement` IS `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained`, `the day of its passing or making` IS NOTHING) BECAUSE "the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained"

§ `Section 2(2): an enactment that has been replaced, has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect is deemed repealed`

#ASSERT     `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has been replaced`
#ASSERT     `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has expired`
#ASSERT     `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has lapsed`
#ASSERT     `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has otherwise ceased to have effect`
#ASSERT NOT `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it still has effect`

§ `Section 3(1): the four Acts repealed, from the commencement of this Act (the end of 31 December 2005)`

#ASSERT     `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1889`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1923`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1937`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation (Amendment) Act 1993`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `another Act`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2005 12 30) `, the Act being` `the Interpretation Act 1889`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2005 12 31) `, the Act being` `the Interpretation Act 1889`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2006 1 1)   `, the Act being` `the Interpretation Act 1889`
#ASSERT     `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2005 12 31) `, the Act being` `the Interpretation (Amendment) Act 1993`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2005 12 30) `, the Act being` `the Interpretation Act 1923`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2026 1 1)   `, the Act being` `another Act`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) has repealed the Act by the end of` (YMD 2005 10 17) `, the Act being` `the Interpretation Act 1937`

§ `Section 3(2): the savings`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for the savings in section 3(2)`
`the savings facts` a b c d MEANS
    `Facts for the savings in section 3(2)` WITH
        `the repealed Act assigns a meaning to a word or expression in another enactment`   IS a
        `the repealed Act provides for another matter in another enactment`                  IS b
        `without that provision in this Act the other enactment would be changed in intent or become unclear or absurd`     IS c
        `applying to the other enactment the corresponding provision of this Act would change it in intent or make it unclear or absurd` IS d

-- (a): a meaning is assigned AND (limb (i) OR limb (ii))
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- (b): another matter AND NOT a meaning AND (limb (i) OR limb (ii))
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`the savings facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`the savings facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`the savings facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`the savings facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- "other than a matter to which paragraph (a) relates": a meaning is dealt with by (a), not (b)
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`the savings facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`the savings facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `Section 26(1): the repealed enactment continues in force until the substituted provisions come into operation`

#ASSERT     `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 5 30) `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT     `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT     `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the substituted provisions being` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `, the substituted provisions being` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT     `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repealed enactment is in force throughout` (YMD 2026 6 2)  `, the substituted provisions being` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§ `Section 26(2)(a): a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act for the remainder of the period`

#ASSERT     `a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, the period for which the person was appointed ending on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the former enactment being repealed and re-enacted` TRUE `, the person having been appointed under it` TRUE
#ASSERT     `a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the period for which the person was appointed ending on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the former enactment being repealed and re-enacted` TRUE `, the person having been appointed under it` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act on` (YMD 2028 1 1) `, the period for which the person was appointed ending on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the former enactment being repealed and re-enacted` TRUE `, the person having been appointed under it` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, the period for which the person was appointed ending on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the former enactment being repealed and re-enacted` FALSE `, the person having been appointed under it` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a person appointed under the former enactment continues to act on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, the period for which the person was appointed ending on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the former enactment being repealed and re-enacted` TRUE `, the person having been appointed under it` FALSE
-- the last day of a period of one year from 1 January 2027 is 31 December 2027, as the module for periods says
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 12 31

§ `Section 26(2)(b): continuing securities, and things prepared or used`

#ASSERT     `the security remains in force` TRUE `the security being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the security remains in force` FALSE `the security being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the security remains in force` TRUE `the security being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `the data, books, papers, forms and things may continue to be used` TRUE `, the things being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the data, books, papers, forms and things may continue to be used` FALSE `, the things being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the data, books, papers, forms and things may continue to be used` TRUE `, the things being` FALSE

§ `Section 26(2)(c): proceedings taken under the former enactment`

#ASSERT     `the proceedings may be continued under the new enactment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be continued under the new enactment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be continued under the new enactment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be continued under the new enactment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be continued under the new enactment` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 26(2)(d): a statutory instrument made under a repealed and re-enacted provision`

-- the re-enactment must come into operation after the commencement of this Act
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the instrument is deemed to have been made under the new provision and remains in force until it is repealed or otherwise ceases to have effect`
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the instrument is deemed to have been made under the new provision only to the extent that it is not inconsistent with the new enactment`
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (d) does not apply`
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (d) does not apply`
-- before the commencement of this Act, or at the same moment as it: not "after"
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2005 6 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (d) does not apply`
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2006 1 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (d) does not apply`
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2006 1 2)) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the instrument is deemed to have been made under the new provision and remains in force until it is repealed or otherwise ceases to have effect`
-- a re-enactment passed on 1 January 2006 with no moment named cannot be placed against the commencement of this Act
#ASSERT REFUSED `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2006 1 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `what paragraph (d) does to the instrument` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2005 12 31)) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (d) does not apply`
-- the results are distinct values
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (d) does not apply` EQUALS `the instrument is deemed to have been made under the new provision only to the extent that it is not inconsistent with the new enactment`)

§ `Section 26(2)(e): a different form of words does not by itself make the idea different`

#ASSERT     `the idea in the new enactment is not taken to be different merely because a different form of words is used` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the idea in the new enactment is not taken to be different merely because a different form of words is used` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the idea in the new enactment is not taken to be different merely because a different form of words is used` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the idea in the new enactment is not taken to be different merely because a different form of words is used` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 26(2)(f): a reference to the former enactment`

#ASSERT `how a reference in any other enactment to the former enactment is read` TRUE TRUE TRUE  EQUALS `as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter`
#ASSERT `how a reference in any other enactment to the former enactment is read` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the former enactment is disregarded in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the other enactment`
#ASSERT `how a reference in any other enactment to the former enactment is read` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (f) does not apply`
#ASSERT `how a reference in any other enactment to the former enactment is read` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (f) does not apply`
#ASSERT `how a reference in any other enactment to the former enactment is read` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (f) does not apply`

§ `Section 27(1)(a): the repeal does not revive what was not in force or not existing immediately before it`

#ASSERT `what section 27(1)(a) says of a thing that` `it was not in force` EQUALS `the repeal does not revive it`
#ASSERT `what section 27(1)(a) says of a thing that` `it did not exist`   EQUALS `the repeal does not revive it`
#ASSERT `what section 27(1)(a) says of a thing that` `it was in force or existing` EQUALS `paragraph (a) does not apply to it`

§ `Section 27(1)(b): previous operation and things duly done or suffered`

#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect a thing done or suffered on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, duly done or suffered under the enactment being` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a thing done or suffered on` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `, duly done or suffered under the enactment being` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a thing done or suffered on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, duly done or suffered under the enactment being` FALSE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the repeal does not affect a thing done or suffered on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, duly done or suffered under the enactment being` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§ `Section 27(1)(c): rights, privileges, obligations and liabilities acquired, accrued or incurred`

#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, under the enactment being` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred on` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `, under the enactment being` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, under the enactment being` FALSE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§ `Section 27(1)(d): penalties, forfeitures and punishments for an offence committed before the repeal`

#ASSERT     `the repeal does not affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment for an offence or contravention committed on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the offence being against the enactment` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment for an offence or contravention committed on` (YMD 2026 6 1)  `, the offence being against the enactment` TRUE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment for an offence or contravention committed on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the offence being against the enactment` FALSE `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§ `Section 27(1)(e): legal proceedings pending at the time of the repeal`

GIVEN began IS A DATE
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
      kind IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about proceedings at a repeal`
`proceedings begun on` began `and ended` ended `, of the kind` kind MEANS
    `Facts about proceedings at a repeal` WITH
        `the day the proceedings began` IS began
        `the day the proceedings ended` IS ended
        `they are in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, offence or contravention of the kind in (c) and (d)` IS kind

-- begun before the repeal and not ended: pending
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not prejudice or affect the legal proceedings` (`proceedings begun on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and ended` NOTHING `, of the kind` TRUE) `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- ended on the last day before the repeal: not pending at the repeal
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not prejudice or affect the legal proceedings` (`proceedings begun on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and ended` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 31)) `, of the kind` TRUE) `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- ended on or after the day the repeal comes into operation: pending at the repeal
#ASSERT     `the repeal does not prejudice or affect the legal proceedings` (`proceedings begun on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and ended` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) `, of the kind` TRUE) `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- begun after the repeal: not pending at it
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not prejudice or affect the legal proceedings` (`proceedings begun on` (YMD 2026 6 2) `and ended` NOTHING `, of the kind` TRUE) `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- not proceedings of the kind the paragraph names
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not prejudice or affect the legal proceedings` (`proceedings begun on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and ended` NOTHING `, of the kind` FALSE) `, the repealing enactment being` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§ `Section 27(2): proceedings and penalties as if the enactment had not been repealed`

#ASSERT     `the proceedings may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the penalty imposed and carried out, as if the enactment had not been repealed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the penalty imposed and carried out, as if the enactment had not been repealed` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the penalty imposed and carried out, as if the enactment had not been repealed` TRUE FALSE
